- op: discuss  # aa40
  at: '2026-10-01T01:07:28Z'  # aa40
  by: agent  # aa40
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aa40
  clock: 4  # aa40
  nonce: aa40  # aa40
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\nMechanism holds: metrics.py:58-59 averages edge `confidence` only; :180 emits round(mean,3); no histogram / median / mode / multimodal flag anywhere in metrics (keys: avg_confidence, by_supply_chain_tier, debug, languages, total_edges, total_files, total_nodes). grep for confidence_hist/_dist/_buckets in packages/*/src: 0 hits. metrics.py history since filing: no change to the confidence line.\nNumbers drifted (self-survey of this repo at 134a06d505, 217,668 edges): avg_confidence 0.746 (was 0.8); 9 distinct values; spikes 0.85 (96,036), 0.4 (34,317), 0.5 (31,755), 0.95 (30,796), 0.9 (21,874), 0.8 (2,427), then 0.7 (379), 0.75 (65), 0.72 (19). Top six = 99.79% of edges. The 1.0 spike (18,388) and the 0.3 type_hierarchy cohort from the filing are gone. Median 0.85 vs mean 0.746: the scalar sits between spikes, on no edge at all.\nThe 2026-06-06 scope facet also holds: 0 of 55,141 nodes carry a `confidence` key; spec section \"Aggregate statistics\" (hypergumbo-spec.md:1347, was cited as §938) still lists avg_confidence with no edges-only qualifier.\nRelated: WI-famiv (ADR-0039 ruling-1 literal-confidence producers) is the producer-side reason the values are spikes.\nProposed update: refresh the counts in the description; the title's \"0.8\" is now 0.746 on the self map."  # aa40
- op: update  # 7ffc
