  set:  # 7ffc
    title: "metrics.avg_confidence (0.746 on the self map) hides a spiked multimodal edge-confidence distribution"  # 7ffc
    description: "**Mechanic**: The top-level scalar `metrics.avg_confidence` (metrics.py:58-59, emitted at :180 as round(mean, 3)) summarizes every edge as a single decimal; metrics carries no histogram, median, mode or multimodality signal. The underlying distribution is a handful of tight spikes — per-evidence-type hardcoded values, not a continuous distribution. On a self-analysis map of this repo (dev 134a06d505, 217,668 edges): avg_confidence 0.746; 9 distinct values; 0.85 (96,036), 0.4 (34,317), 0.5 (31,755), 0.95 (30,796), 0.9 (21,874), 0.8 (2,427), then 0.7 (379), 0.75 (65), 0.72 (19). The top six are 99.79% of edges. Median 0.85; the mean sits between spikes, on no edge at all.\n\n**Scope (second facet, F90.A2)**: the average is over EDGES ONLY — 0 of 55,141 nodes carry a `confidence` key — yet spec \"Aggregate statistics\" (hypergumbo-spec.md:1347) lists avg_confidence with no edges-only qualifier.\n\n**Expectation**: The reported summary statistic reflects the distribution shape — an additional histogram field, a mode/median, or a multimodal flag — and states what it averages, so a consumer is not misled into treating a spiked distribution as smooth or as whole-map confidence.\n\n**Exposure**: Any dashboard reporting \"this analysis has avg confidence 0.75\"; any consumer doing `confidence > avg_confidence` slicing.\n\n**Consequence**: Dashboards imply a centered distribution; slicing on `avg_confidence` cuts between spike values and produces nondeterministic-feeling thresholds.\n\n**Related**: WI-famiv (ADR-0039 ruling-1 literal-confidence producers) is the producer-side reason the values are spikes.\n\n**Source**: F49.A4 (INDEPENDENT, HIGH). Filed via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`.\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 7ffc
- op: discuss  # bd3e
  at: '2026-10-01T23:46:45Z'  # bd3e
  by: agent  # bd3e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bd3e
  clock: 6  # bd3e
  nonce: bd3e  # bd3e
  message: "IMPLEMENTED (concurrent run 2026-10-01, local branch jgstern-agent/feat/zimor-edge-confidence-distribution, commit 2eab038864, worktree ~/hg_wt/zimor; not pushed). Status not changed.\nChange: metrics gains edge_confidence = {histogram, median}. histogram = edge count per confidence value at 0.01 resolution, keys \"%.2f\", ascending (bounded to 101 keys on [0,1]; producers that multiply confidences, e.g. haskell/scala 0.85*lookup*penalty, fold into their 0.01 bucket). median = LOWER median, so always a value some edge carries; null (not 0.0) when no edge carries confidence. avg_confidence value unchanged. Its schema description and spec \"metrics\" section now say EDGES ONLY, and that its 0.0 with no edges is a placeholder. Generator scripts/generate-schema; docs/schema.json regenerated; SCHEMA_VERSION NOT bumped (integrator).\nTests: 6 new tests (5 in test_metrics.py, 1 in test_schema.py), red first (6 failed / 54 passed). Targeted smart-test, 481 files: 16,636 passed, 1 failed, 100% coverage on metrics.py. The one failure was test_a_hangup_is_named_too: WI-narum, caused by my nohup launch (see the note there).\nLive repro, coredns (worktree code via slot survey, 27 s): total_edges 21,994, all carrying confidence; nodes with a confidence key: 0. avg_confidence 0.717. edge_confidence.histogram {0.40: 6337, 0.49: 87, 0.50: 769, 0.57: 180, 0.65: 7, 0.70: 157, 0.72: 682, 0.75: 135, 0.80: 1338, 0.85: 6389, 0.90: 2417, 0.95: 3496}, median 0.85. An independent recount from edges[] matches exactly. Bimodal: 0.40 is 28.8% and 0.85 is 29.1% of edges. On coredns the mean (0.717) rounds onto a minor real spike (0.72, 3.1% of edges), so \"the mean sits on no edge\" is a self-map observation, not a general one.\nNOT done: no multimodal flag or mode field (both derivable from the histogram); avg_confidence is still 0.0 with no edges (kept for backward compatibility; the empty histogram and null median disclose it); the self map was not re-surveyed.\nResidual filed: WI-susas-vigov-kurah-pumir-ragit-hatiz-likur-disal. The spec still defines total_files as the profile sum (P3, docs)."  # bd3e
